[176.371047, "o", "md.sh /app/jq_args.yaml — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash ls -lh /app/active_users_report.json /app/cmd.sh /app/jq_args.yaml\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  glimmer-30b — 51 tool call(s) so far\r\nAll tasks completed.\r\n\r\n**Files created:**\r\n- `/app/active_users_report.json` – 346 active users, sorted by username, with fields `user_id`, `username`, `email`, `last_login` (YYYY-MM-DD), `role_count`, `primary_role` (null when roles empty). Output is 2-space indented JSON array.\r\n- `/app/cmd.sh` – contains the exact jq command used:\r\n  ```\r\n  jq 'map(select(.status==\"active\") | {user_id:.id, username:.username, email:.email, last_login:(.last_login|split(\"T\")[0]), role_count:(.roles|length), primary_role:(.roles[0])}) | sort_by(.username)' /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json\r\n  ```\r\n- `/app/jq_args.yaml` – filter and empty args list as required.\r\n\r\nVerification:\r\n- Count = 346 active users\r\n- All objects have required keys\r\n- `last_login` matches `^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$`\r\n- `primary_role` is string or null\r\n- Us"]
